### PLM API walkthrough for VS Code's "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client).
### Start the stack first: `make up` then `make run`. Run the requests top to bottom.
### IntelliJ's HTTP client uses different syntax for chaining requests: use the curl walkthrough instead.

@api = http://localhost:8080/api/v1
@token = http://localhost:8180/realms/plm/protocol/openid-connect/token
@partType = 00000000-0000-7000-8000-000000000102
@bobId = b0b00000-0000-4000-8000-000000000002
@carolId = ca201000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003

### 0a. Sign in as alice (site admin)
# @name alice
POST {{token}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=plm-web&username=alice&password=alice

### 0b. Sign in as bob
# @name bob
POST {{token}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=plm-web&username=bob&password=bob

### 0c. Sign in as carol
# @name carol
POST {{token}}
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=password&client_id=plm-web&username=carol&password=carol

### 1. Who am I?
GET {{api}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.access_token}}

### 2. The site (root) context
# @name site
GET {{api}}/contexts/site
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.access_token}}

### 3. Alice creates an organization
# @name org
POST {{api}}/contexts
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "parentId": "{{site.response.body.id}}", "kind": "ORGANIZATION", "name": "Acme {{$guid}}" }

### 4. ...and a product inside it
# @name product
POST {{api}}/contexts
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "parentId": "{{org.response.body.id}}", "kind": "PRODUCT", "name": "Drone X1" }

### 5. Alice puts bob on the product team as a MEMBER
PUT {{api}}/contexts/{{product.response.body.id}}/members/{{bobId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "MEMBER" }

### 6. What may bob do here? -> CREATE, MODIFY, READ, REVISE
GET {{api}}/contexts/{{product.response.body.id}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.access_token}}

### 7. Bob creates a part -> A.1
# @name part
POST {{api}}/objects
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "typeId": "{{partType}}",
  "contextId": "{{product.response.body.id}}",
  "name": "Motor mount",
  "attributes": { "material": "AL6061", "massKg": 0.12 }
}

### 8. Bob checks it out -> working copy A.2
POST {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.access_token}}

### 9. Alice tries too -> 409 ALREADY_CHECKED_OUT (by Bob Builder)
POST {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/checkout
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.access_token}}

### 10. Carol is not on the team -> 404
GET {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{carol.response.body.access_token}}

### 11. Bob edits the working copy
PATCH {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/working-copy
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "attributes": { "material": "Ti-6Al-4V", "massKg": 0.09 } }

### 12. Bob checks in -> A.2 is now the latest, immutable iteration
POST {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/checkin
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.access_token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "comment": "Switch to titanium" }

### 13. Bob revises -> B.1
POST {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/revise
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.access_token}}

### 14. History, newest first: B.1, A.2, A.1
GET {{api}}/objects/{{part.response.body.id}}/iterations
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.access_token}}

### 15. Everything bob can read in the product
GET {{api}}/objects?contextId={{product.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{bob.response.body.access_token}}

### 16. Alice reads the audit trail for the part
GET {{api}}/audit?aggregateId={{part.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{alice.response.body.access_token}}
